; Isolates the `@ignore` comment-DSL directive in both container reps: the open struct-map
; tolerate-and-drop rest ROW (`ignored`) and the open-array tolerate-and-drop rest TAIL
; (`ignored_list`). Unknown trailing data is typed-deserialized (for a map, key AND value; for an
; array, each element — so the stream advances) and then DROPPED — no `rest` field is generated, and
; serialize re-emits only the declared members / prefix. Rejected under --preserve-encodings (a
; preserve crate's byte-exact contract cannot hold for a deliberately lossy type), so this fixture is
; generation-skipped under the preserve profile (registered in snapshot_tests::PROFILE_GENERATION_SKIP
; and feature_corpus_compiles's EXPECTED_GENERATION_FAIL); default/json generate the closed-struct
; surface.
;
; The `; @ignore` must sit on its own line before the container's closing token: a CDDL comment runs
; to the end of the line, so `; @ignore }` would swallow the map's brace and `; @ignore ]` the array's
; bracket.
ignored = {
  1: uint,
  * uint => text ; @ignore
}

ignored_list = [
  uint,
  * uint ; @ignore
]
